But actually, for a horizontal bar chart, the reference line represents a specific TIME value. Different modules have different reference times, so each reference line is at a different x position. But the line spans the full height, which means it shows the reference time for ALL modules at once. This is visually confusing.

A better approach: draw a short marker line near each bar, or add a colored dot at the reference value on each bar.

